  clock: 4  # 716d
  nonce: 716d  # 716d
  message: "Done in PR #1078 (dev a7495d9b9a + d2b8c8f349). The instrument is `hypergumbo backend-agreement ARTIFACT [--format md|json] [--out FILE]` (hypergumbo_core/backend_agreement.py). It reads ONE survey artifact's own provenance — `attribution` / `alternatives` on merged records (WI-binis's §6 slot), `origin_run_id` → `analysis_runs[].pass` on single-producer ones, folded edges' attribution, `confidence_source == corroborated`, `meta.superseded_by` — so it re-pairs nothing and cannot disagree with the merge pass about what \"the same declaration\" is. A producer is what the registry declares for the language, incumbent first (`incumbent_first`); a linker's or the merge pass's own records are not a producer's. Per language with two producers: pairing by kind; per-attribute agree / disagree / one-sided counts with the disagreement shapes (spans as line:col-line:col; `stable_id` counted, not exemplified); edge overlap per edge type split by resolution; corroborated and superseded counts. Markdown is the committed docs/audits/ sibling form (`kind: backend_agreement`; the verdicts lint now reads a document's declared kind via `audit_findings.declared_kind` and skips siblings); --format json for a machine reader.\n\nBehavioural evidence: `hypergumbo backend-agreement <two-arm artifact>` exits 0 and prints the table (test_backend_agreement.py::TestTheSubcommand, 3 tests: stdout md, --format json --out, exit 2 on a missing/unparseable artifact naming the file). On a synthetic two-producer artifact every table is pinned (8 tests); on the recorded aardvark-dns fixture the instrument reproduces the merge pass's numbers (test_recorded_fixtures.py::TestTheAgreementInstrumentOnBothArms: 148/169 paired, kind 133/15 with shape variable←constant x15, is_exported 107/41 null←false x41, name 83/65, span 2/146, stable_id 0/134 + 14 one-sided, calls both 93 = corroborated, 269 references scip-only, 244 stub calls ts-only, 3 superseded) and the committed docs/audits/0019 YAML block + per-attribute rows are asserted equal to what the instrument says today. Six mutations (pairing threshold, agree threshold, resolved flip, opaque skip, corroborated match, producer filter) each kill 1–9 tests.\n\nThe first table, docs/audits/0019-backend-agreement-rust-aardvark-dns.md, is produced from the §12 recorded fixture by scripts/regenerate-backend-agreement-table (live tree-sitter arm + recorded rust-analyzer 1.94.0 index → merge → dedup → resolution verdict → supersession, `_two_arm_artifact()` in the fixture tests) — no rust-analyzer install and no build.rs execution needed, and no ADR-0045 trust grant for the fixture crate, which is why it is not a live `hypergumbo survey` of the crate. The script preserves the hand-written `## Reading`.\n\nWhat the table changes: nothing — and that is the finding. No per-attribute exception is warranted today: `kind`'s 15 are WI-bamar (rust.py's const→variable; fix the producer, §7); `name`'s 65 are the Type::member vs member vocabulary question (owner's, not precedence); `is_exported`'s 41 are the incumbent's None beating a concrete False — filed as INV-huboz against arbitrate() (an absent value is not a candidate), not a precedence exception; `stable_id`'s 14 one-sided are the SCIP arm emitting no stable_id on struct/enum/trait — WI-paluk. The one-sided qualified_name/signature/docstring/modifiers columns say the SCIP translation fills none of them, so nothing can be measured there yet.\n\nAlso fixed in the same PR, found by its CI: INV-ziruv — run_survey's global file index outlived a run that raised after indexing (the merge pass's refusal), so the next run_all_analyzers on the same xdist worker read another repository's files. finally-decorator `cli._releases_file_index`; reproduced locally in CI's order (2 failed → 92 passed).\n\nNot asserted: the table's numbers on any repository other than the recorded fixture; whether SCIP's `constant` should win kind before WI-bamar lands (it should not — the producer fix makes the disagreement vanish)."  # 716d
